codex
Implemented a native Track B generator based on Theorems 2.3/3.2 and Lemma 4.1 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1906.05611).

Local results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: 0/8 each.
- Reference elimination: 24,678 operations average, 8/8 solved.
- Intended circulant route: 204 operations.
- Canonicalization: 60/60 invariance checks; 20/20 distinct seeds.
- Worst measured answer: 576 characters, 97 elements.

Files:

- [gen_1906_05611.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.05611/gen_1906_05611.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.05611/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.05611/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.05611/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.05611/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.05611/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The remaining blocker is external: every OpenRouter call returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” leaving all oracle arms at 0 scored attempts. Consequently STEP 4 is not verified and `submit.sh` correctly blocks submission. I did not fabricate evidence or reject the paper.
