  • Finalize reports and README from measured results
codex
The prior build’s theorem use is basically sound, but its claimed hardness is not: the displayed equations are sparse, so a natural recurrence propagation recovers the witness in \(O(d)\), essentially the same work as the advertised “compact” route. I’m replacing that disguise with the finite-field Fourier coordinate change. It is still a native projective transformation from the paper’s LP vertex, but it turns the Frobenius cycle diagonal and the equations dense: generic elimination is genuinely cubic, while the structural route is one coordinatewise invariant with about \(d\) operations.
