 ## Caveats
 
-- This family is deliberately easy for a computer with modular elimination; its claim is only Track B.  The 0.021-second mean reference time is evidence of that honesty, not Track-A hardness.
-- The generated vertices have equations over the distinguished base field and one binomial circulant disguise.  They do not sample arbitrary vertices over \(GF(q^d)\).
-- The 0/200,000 estimate uses the exact declared prior—uniform normalized base-field projective points.  It demonstrates guess resistance, not a statistical upper bound on every informed heuristic.
-- The panel tests coordinate scores, a sparse-nullspace greedy choice, 256 random restarts, and constant/axis ansatzes.  It does not test every possible circulant-factorization heuristic; recognizing the circulant is the intended route.
-- `canonical_key` removes generated circulant/cyclic disguises and keys on the LP norm up to inversion.  Additional projective equivalences outside those tested could make it over-distinguish; full projective equivalence classification is not attempted.
-- Local G, V, density, attack, scaling, and canonicalization gates pass.  H against the required model pool remains unverified solely because the external OpenRouter key had exhausted its limit.
+- Modular elimination solves this family efficiently with tools; only the no-tool compression gap is claimed.
+- The generator samples Fourier transforms of the paper's displayed LP vertices with \(\delta\in GF(q)\), not arbitrary vertices over \(GF(q^d)\). It also chooses \(q\equiv1\pmod d\) so the Fourier eigenbasis is defined over the base field.
+- The 0/200,000 estimate uses the exact declared prior—uniform projective points already in \(\Gamma\). It establishes resistance to uninformed guessing under that prior, not against the root-of-unity insight.
+- The failing panel tests coordinate-support outliers, a sparse three-coordinate nullspace, 256 structure-aware random restarts, and constant/axis ansatzes. The root-of-unity power-sum method is intentionally the successful reference insight; no claim is made against all structured symbolic attacks.
+- `canonical_key` removes coordinate/eigenvalue permutations and equation-basis changes and identifies \(\delta\) with \(\delta^{-1}\). Full projective-semilinear equivalence classification is not attempted, so the key may over-distinguish further equivalent vertices.
+- Most importantly, no oracle response was scored. Local G and V are verified; the required model-pool evidence for H must still be collected.
